1
00:00:00,052 --> 00:00:03,022
(Sheldon:)Mrs. Wunch in fourth grade.

2
00:00:04,089 --> 00:00:05,689
(Sheldon:)And my slogan was
“a line that's straight

3
00:00:05,691 --> 00:00:07,861
is a line that's great”"

4
00:00:09,028 --> 00:00:10,598
(Man:)Is this guy for real?

5
00:00:10,596 --> 00:00:14,266
(Leonard:)Boy, I wish
I could say no.

6
00:00:15,401 --> 00:00:18,301
(Beverly:)That was very nice
of Sheldon to apologize.

7
00:00:18,304 --> 00:00:20,404
(Amy:)Well, he's come a long way.

8
00:00:20,406 --> 00:00:23,006
(Amy:)Or a short way very slowly,

9
00:00:23,008 --> 00:00:26,448
(Amy:)so it feels like a long way.

10
00:00:26,445 --> 00:00:29,145
(Beverly:)Your relationship
with him is fascinating.

11
00:00:29,148 --> 00:00:32,078
(Beverly:)I'm preparing to write a book
on high-achieving couples,

12
00:00:32,084 --> 00:00:34,014
(Beverly:)and I would love to
interview the both of you.

13
00:00:34,019 --> 00:00:35,419
(Amy:)Oh, sure.

14
00:00:35,421 --> 00:00:37,221
I'll-I'll talk
to Sheldon about it.

15
00:00:37,222 --> 00:00:39,292
(Amy:)You know, Bernadette's husband
is a former astronaut.

16
00:00:39,291 --> 00:00:41,061
(Beverly:)Really?

17
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:42,160
(Beverly:)Do you think
he would be interested

18
00:00:42,161 --> 00:00:43,391
(Beverly:)in being interviewed
as well?

19
00:00:43,395 --> 00:00:44,925
(Bernadette:)Do I think he'd be interested?

20
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:46,830
(Bernadette:)Sometimes I hear him
pretending to be interviewed

21
00:00:46,832 --> 00:00:48,802
(Bernadette:)when he's alone
in the bathroom.

22
00:00:48,801 --> 00:00:50,801
Wonderful!

23
00:00:50,803 --> 00:00:53,073
(Amy:)I'll give you
my contact information.

24
00:00:54,173 --> 00:00:57,273
(Bernadette:)Um, you should probably
talk to Penny, too.

25
00:00:57,276 --> 00:01:01,026
(Beverly:)About what?

